            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0325" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/777: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-31T15:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 1, 1921—11:18
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>489. I am reliably informed that the Mexican Supreme Court by unanimous vote has
                    denied <hi rendition="#italic">amparos</hi> asked for by several American oil
                    companies against denouncement made by third parties on lots leased by companies
                    prior to May 1st 1917.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
